DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions return a pointer to the ELF Compression Header data
     structure associated with section descriptor _s_c_n.

     Function eellff3322__ggeettcchhddrr() retrieves a pointer to an _E_l_f_3_2___C_h_d_r structure.
     Section descriptor _s_c_n must be associated with an ELF descriptor of class
     ELFCLASS32.

     Function eellff6644__ggeettcchhddrr() retrieves a pointer to an _E_l_f_6_4___C_h_d_r structure.
     Section descriptor _s_c_n must be associated with an ELF descriptor of class
     ELFCLASS64.

     Function ggeellff__ggeettcchhddrr() copies the values in the compression header asso‐
     ciated with argument _s_c_n to the structure pointed to be argument _d_s_t.
     The _G_E_l_f___C_h_d_r data structure is described in gelf(3).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Functions eellff3322__ggeettcchhddrr() and eellff6644__ggeettcchhddrr() return a valid pointer to
     the appropriate compression header on success or NULL if an error was en‐
     countered.

     Function ggeellff__ggeettcchhddrr() returns argument _d_s_t if successful, or NULL if an
     error was encountered.

